  "input" : "Computer Networks Basics Chapter 1: Introduction to Computer Networks Computer networks connect multiple computers for resource sharing. Network Types: LAN, MAN, WAN OSI Model: 7 layers - Physical, Data Link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, Application TCP/IP Protocol Stack: Application, Transport, Internet, Link Chapter 2: Physical Layer Transmission media: Twisted pair, Fiber optic, Wireless Chapter 3: Data Link Layer Ethernet is the most common LAN technology. Frame structure and error detection. Chapter 4: Network Layer IP protocol provides connectionless, unreliable delivery. Routing algorithms: Distance vector (RIP), Link state (OSPF) Chapter 5: Transport Layer TCP: Reliable, connection-oriented protocol UDP: Unreliable, connectionless protocol References: Kurose & Ross, Computer Networking, 8th ed.",
